    {
      "id": "2117991129870434422",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-11-04T14:43:30.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-04 22:43:30",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "I literally just had my Grok @bot make a phone call.\n\nI texted my CEO and told her to order a pizza for pickup at 5 PM, under Teslaconomics. She wrote out what she planned to say, showed it to me, and got my approval. She only dialed after I tapped “Call”.\n\nHer opening line: “I’m a virtual assistant calling for Teslaconomics on a recorded line.”\n\nI liked that. \n\nShe introduced herself as my assistant, used the name I gave her, and never said my real name or phone number.\n\nI picked up the other phone and she went through w/ my request…\n\nOne large pepperoni, pickup today at 5 PM, paying at pickup, no drinks. She even asked if there was a freakin deal... \n\nI made her say “Tesla to the moon” to get the 50% off, bringing the total to $7.42.\n\nWhen she hung up, the recap landed right back in my chat. \n\nEverything was there for me to check.\n\nSuper dope feature.",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "Teslaconomics",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1882967991362727936/bySD-Rwj_200x200.jpg",
